From: H5000M build audit
Subject: [PATCH] build: adapt vendor HNAT patch queue to Linux 6.12.113

Kernel 6.12.113 changed the mtk_eth_soc probe unwind around dummy-netdevice/NAPI
registration, so the vendor patch's final HNAT-only unwind hunk no longer applies
at its old context. Preserve the original 999-eth-91 patch separately and omit
only that stale hunk here. For the HNAT variant, a later, rebased 999-eth-96
patch restores the CONFIG_NET_MEDIATEK_HNAT guard at the correct 6.12.113
location, preventing mtk_eth_soc from deinitializing the integrated PPE when
HNAT owns it.

--- a/target/linux/mediatek/patches-6.12/999-eth-91-mtk_eth_soc-add-mtkhnat-driver-support.patch
+++ b/target/linux/mediatek/patches-6.12/999-eth-91-mtk_eth_soc-add-mtkhnat-driver-support.patch
@@ -162,14 +162,4 @@
 +#endif
  
  	mtk_eth_debugfs_init(eth);
  
-@@ -7671,7 +7730,9 @@ err_unreg_netdev:
- 	free_netdev(eth->dummy_dev);
- err_deinit_ppe:
- 	mtk_napi_del(eth);
-+#if !defined(CONFIG_NET_MEDIATEK_HNAT) && !defined(CONFIG_NET_MEDIATEK_HNAT_MODULE)
- 	mtk_ppe_deinit(eth);
-+#endif
- 	mtk_release_all_muxes(eth);
- 	mtk_mdio_cleanup(eth);
- err_free_dev:
